{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876344-neter-khertet-and-the-wider-cofd-setting","id":876344,"title":"Neter-Khertet and the wider CofD setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-28T01:11:04-07:00","id":876344,"title":"Neter-Khertet and the wider CofD setting","content":"Forgive me if I'm wrong, but is Mummy the only game that treats Twilight as a separate realm rather than just a transitory state of being? <br /> <br /> Other gamelines treat Twilight as a hazy layer of reality that includes the ephemeral, while Mummy bestows it with landmarks in the form of the mountains at the edges of the horizon. What does this mean? Could there possibly be creatures native to Nerter-Khertet? Sorry if this is incoherent, but it seems to be a unique and overlooked facet of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:17:01-07:00","id":876384,"title":"","content":"Oddly enough, I have been open to the idea that the Twilight is more than it appears to be. Heck, I wouldn't mind a setting hack which expands it into something like <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Watch_(Lukyanenko_novel)\" target=\"_blank\">the Twilight in this book</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#po