v class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876344-neter-khertet-and-the-wider-cofd-setting?p=876385#post876385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the posts and threads I'm seeing active lately you're all really going to love the Cleopatra chapter in the DE Companion.<br /> <br /> I kinda think amkhata could be considered native to it, but surely there are things that, if not exactly native, might be stuck there in a kind of limbo. Maybe the Mutapa chapter will provide insight but yeah &amp;quot;native to Twilight&amp;quot; was something I specifically requested for Cleopatra.<br /> <br /> Now stop setting me up to break unofficial quasi NDAs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>How soon CAN we expect the Companion supplement to arrive? And speaking of Amkhata, was there ever any tidbit that describes them forming 'naturally' besides via sundered relics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:34:11-07:00","id":876400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876344-neter-khertet-and-the-wider-cofd-setting#post876344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if I'm wrong, but is Mummy the only game that treats Twilight as a separate realm rather than just a transitory state of being?<br /> <br /> Other gamelines treat Twilight as a hazy layer of reality that includes the ephemeral, while Mummy bestows it with landmarks in the form of the mountains at the edges of the horizon. What does this mean? Could there possibly be creatures native to Nerter-Khertet? Sorry if this is incoherent, but it seems to be a unique and overlooked facet of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies have an expansive perspective on Neter-Khertet due to their particular observations of how it works, even when others might call part of it (Twilight) a &quot;state.&quot; The Mutapa chapter discusses this in some detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T03:45:02-07:00","id":876437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876344-neter-khertet-and-the-wider-cofd-setting?p=876395#post876395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm increasingly worried that we're somehow the same person, reseru.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...<i>share </i>your sentiments <i>exactly</i>.<br /> <br /> dun dun DUN!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T21:12:34-07:00","id":924283,"title":"","content":"So to bring this thread back; what could be native to Netwr-Khertet? It could be that amkhat are &quot;naturally&quot;' disembodied and that the ritual to create one actually just gives it a physical form. Are the Slaughterers that the Iremites so feared only found in Duat, or could they (and other demons who are tragically not knife-wielding) be found there as well? We know the Arisen see the mountains of the East and West in Neter-Khert, but could the &quot;Isle of Flame&quot; often described in Egyptian texts be there as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:02:44-07:00","id":924412,"title":"","content":"Before the arrival of second edition, I had assumed that the Arisen's perception of Twilight was an effect of the Rite of Return: a mystically-induced Jerusalem Syndrome meant to reinforce certain religious beliefs.<br /> <br /> I think maybe ghosts who've been blessed or cursed by Iremite magics could become native to Neter-Kkhertet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T10:09:02-07:00","id":924512,"title":"","content":"Would Anpu be considered a native of Neter-Khertet? Maybe Sha, or a later analog of them? Deceived in Henet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T08:59:23-07:00","id":924898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876344-neter-khertet-and-the-wider-cofd-setting?p=876385#post876385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the posts and threads I'm seeing active lately you're all really going to love the Cleopatra chapter in the DE Companion.<br /> <br /> I kinda think amkhata could be considered native to it, but surely there are things that, if not exactly native, might be stuck there in a kind of limbo. Maybe the Mutapa chapter will provide insight but yeah &quot;native to Twilight&quot; was something I specifically requested for Cleopatra.<br /> <br /> Now stop setting me up to break unofficial quasi NDAs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm watching you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:33:58-07:00","id":926149,"title":"","content":"Well, G-M angels are native to the Twilight-state Phenomenal world, so it's possible that other, vaguely similar beings might be native to the &quot;deeper&quot; Twilight of Mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T21:18:44-07:00","id":927439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876344-neter-khertet-and-the-wider-cofd-setting?p=876395#post876395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm increasingly worried that we're somehow the same person, reseru.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So which one of you is the temakh then?<br /> <br /> Anyway...one way to ask the question is why Mummy treats Twilight as &quot;more&quot; than the other settings. My preferred questioning is why it took so long for a WOD setting to do the concept of Twilight any kind of justice! I mean, Geist was supposedly the setting based around ghosts, right? And yet Twilight, the default state of existence for ghosts, is treated as so uninteresting it gets one brief sidebar in the entire game basically devoted to talking about how uninteresting it is. Mummy is THE game that has done anything remotely cool with Twilight. Which is reason 174 to love this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T21:25:53-07:00","id":927441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876344-neter-khertet-and-the-wider-cofd-setting?p=927439#post927439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So which one of you is the temakh then?<br /> <br /> Anyway...one way to ask the question is why Mummy treats Twilight as &amp;quot;more&amp;quot; than the other settings. My preferred questioning is why it took so long for a WOD setting to do the concept of Twilight any kind of justice! I mean, Geist was supposedly the setting based around ghosts, right? And yet Twilight, the default state of existence for ghosts, is treated as so uninteresting it gets one brief sidebar in the entire game basically devoted to talking about how uninteresting it is. Mummy is THE game that has done anything remotely cool with Twilight. Which is reason 174 to love this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy kind of prides itself on breaking the rules: the power stat starts high and drops, morality starts low and rises, characters are powerful at creation, fiddling with target numbers, making Twilight important, having a set backstory...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T15:09:06-07:00","id":927796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/876344-neter-khertet-and-the-wider-cofd-setting?p=927441#post927441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy kind of prides itself on breaking the rules: the power stat starts high and drops, morality starts low and rises, characters are powerful at creation, fiddling with target numbers, making Twilight important, having a set backstory...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. Also, lifts heavily from Wraith and Orpheus (and Mummy: The Resurrection, of course, although mostly by taking their concepts and asking &quot;How can we make this bleaker, darker, and horrifying?). As far as what might be in Mummy Twilight, my first suggestion is to reread that source material and ask yourself how you can dip the concept in Egyptian Mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}